NPCs: {
	TrashTr0m: {
		DisplayName: Trash-Tr0m
		Epithet: Colossus of the Scrapheap
		Bestiary: The top half of a construction titan, torn off at the waist and welded back together from whatever the Junkyard had. It drags itself after anything that moves, slams the ground hard enough to make it ripple, and inhales whatever it cannot catch. It sleeps under the scrap, guarding a cache it can no longer open: it swallowed the key long ago.
		CacheGuarded: The cache won't budge. Something is still guarding it...
		KeyDropped: A chewed-up key clatters out of the wreck...
		CacheLocked: The cache is locked tight. Trash-Tr0m's Lost Key opens it.
	}

	DeliveryDrone: {
		DisplayName: Delivery Drone
		Bestiary: A delivery drone that lost its route and found a new trade. It circles anything left lying on the ground, scans it for five long seconds and flies off with it in its claw. It is all cardboard and bluster: shoot it down and whatever it took falls back out.
	}

	RustCollector: {
		DisplayName: Rust Collector
		Bestiary: A scrap bin on two rollers that never stopped doing its job. It charges at anything that might be rust, and it thinks everything might be rust. It cannot climb, but it never stops accelerating.
	}

	Trapper: {
		DisplayName: Trapper
		Bestiary: Half goblin, half clockwork, all hunter. It bolted a brass arm and a lens eye onto itself and took to the jungle with a sack of spike balls. It never lets its prey get close: it runs, turns, and seeds the ground with spikes.
	}

	LivingTar: {
		DisplayName: Living Tar
		Bestiary: Tar from the Junkyard pool that crawled out on its own. It hops like any slime, and every landing flings a hot glob of itself at whoever it is chasing.
	}

	RogueMiceBot: {
		DisplayName: Rogue Mice-bot
		Bestiary: A clockwork mouse that slipped its winding key and never came back. The Mech Army winds them up by the dozen; they race in faster than you can walk and pounce with their steel teeth bared.
	}

	Boombot: {
		DisplayName: Boombot
		Bestiary: A bomb with legs and one job. It beeps faster the closer it gets, and the moment it touches you it goes off. Shot down first, it only fizzles.
	}

	AnnoyOTron: {
		DisplayName: Annoy-o-tron
		Bestiary: An alarm box on treads with a spinning emergency beacon for a head. It never fights. It follows the army around, screaming, and every machine that hears it moves half again as fast.
	}

	Jaeger: {
		DisplayName: Jaeger
		Bestiary: The Mech Army's walking fortress, six times taller than a person and armoured like a boiler. It marches slowly and never stops, and whatever it walks into is thrown across the field. It only takes the field once the battle is half won.
	}

	TarTyrant: {
		DisplayName: Tar Tyrant
		Epithet: Monarch of the Mire
		Bestiary: The Junkyard's tar pool is older than the Junkyard. Something enormous drowned in it long ago, and the tar kept its bones and learned to move them. It wears the old skull as a face, flings its own bones at whatever comes near, and every wound it takes sheds tar that crawls off on its own. Only a worm made of scrap is tempting enough to fish it out.
	}

	TarTyrantBubble: {
		DisplayName: Tar Bubble
	}

	ScrapwormCritter: {
		DisplayName: Scrapworm
		Bestiary: A worm that ate so much buried scrap it turned into scrap itself. It is harmless and rare, and something in the Junkyard's tar would very much like to eat it.
	}

	PuxaFrango: {
		DisplayName: Puxa-frango
		Bestiary: A hunched, creaking machine that stalks the caves on spindly legs. It used to guard a henhouse; now it guards nothing and grabs everything. When its claws open wide, it is about to lunge, and it pulls whatever it catches in close.
	}

	Coghawk: {
		DisplayName: Coghawk
		Bestiary: A hawk of brass and riveted iron, wound up round the cog in its chest. It circles high over the dunes until it has picked its prey, screeches once, and drops into a swoop that skims the sand. Whatever stays on the ground gets the talons.
	}

	Splasher: {
		DisplayName: Splasher
		Bestiary: A boiler robot that rusts if it so much as looks at a cloud, so somebody bolted an umbrella to its head. It only comes out in the rain, keeps its distance, pumps its water gun and soaks whoever is out in the storm with it.
	}

	BeatBoxer: {
		DisplayName: Beat-Boxer
		Bestiary: A sparring robot wired to a jukebox, still waiting for the next bout in the halls of the Dungeon. It keeps time on the speakers bolted to its shoulders and throws its spring-loaded gloves in pairs, one-two, hard enough to send you flying.
	}

	Friendobo: {
		DisplayName: Friendo-bot
		Bestiary: An old bartender robot in a top hat and a monocle. He kept a saloon somewhere long ago, and he is still polishing the same glass. He moved in once the Mech Army stopped marching, and he trades in scrap and in the trinkets that wake the big machines.
		Chat1: Welcome, welcome! Mind the floor, I polished it this century.
		Chat2: What'll it be? I've got rusted cogs, rusted scrap and more rusted cogs.
		Chat3: This monocle? Pure brass. The eye behind it, less so.
		Chat4: I used to tend bar in a town down under the desert. Brass everywhere. Then the sand came in, and the customers stopped coming out.
		Chat5: Careful with that top hat, friend. There's a spare spring in it.
		Chat6: Every machine that wakes up angry had something that called it. I sell those, once you have beaten the beast yourself.
		ChatTavernkeep: The Tavernkeep and I trade tips. He says my ale tastes like oil. It is oil.
		ChatMechanic: The Mechanic offered to oil my joints. Kind of them. A bit too eager with the wrench, though.
	}

	Cogtuna: {
		DisplayName: Cogtuna
		Bestiary: A great tuna of riveted iron that never has to surface: a boiler breathes for it, and the furnace in its throat glows whenever it opens its jaws. Its plates turn most blades aside, it hits like a dropped anchor, and it will not leave the water to chase you.
	}

	BrassBandit: {
		DisplayName: Brass Bandit
		Bestiary: An outlaw robot of dusty brass that still holds up the streets of Westworld. It shoots on sight, fans all six chambers of its rusty revolver, then turns tail and runs to reload. Even a bandit knows when it is out of bullets.
	}

	Sheriff: {
		DisplayName: Sheriff
		Bestiary: The last lawman of Westworld, still keeping the peace long after the townsfolk left. Three sheriff stars ride over his hat; he throws them one at a time at whoever breaks the law, and the ones that miss bite into the walls until he calls them home, straight through anyone in the way. His revolver is the only clean thing left in town. He never runs, not even to reload.
	}

	MechanicalBull: {
		DisplayName: Mechanical Bull
		Bestiary: A steam rodeo bull that threw its last rider decades ago and never stopped bucking. When it lowers its horns and paws the ground, get out of the way: once it starts its charge it does not turn.
	}

	Dinamitrom: {
		DisplayName: Dinamitrom
		Bestiary: A powder keg that somebody gave legs. It hops around the old mine with its fuse lit, and when it spots you it crouches and leaps. Shoot it before it lands.
	}

	CursedConductor: {
		DisplayName: Cursed Conductor
		Epithet: The Last Stop
		Bestiary: The conductor of the line that once ran under Westworld, still keeping time for a train that left the rails a hundred years ago. The crash took his legs and the curse took the rest; a turbine bolted where his legs were pumps soot to keep him aloft, and his whistle still calls the train, and the train still comes. Leave his town and he will chase you to the end of the line.
	}

	ConductorGhost: {
		DisplayName: Cursed Ghost
	}

	JadeGolem: {
		DisplayName: Jade Golem
		Bestiary: A statue carved from a single block of jade and woken by the bronze heart set in its chest. It walks slowly and hits like a landslide; when it stops and raises its fist, the light gathering there aims where you stood a moment ago. Keep moving, and move again when the line blinks.
	}
	RhinoBeetle: {
		DisplayName: Rhino Beetle
		Bestiary: A giant rhinoceros beetle of the deep jungle, rarely seen and heavily armoured, spores glowing in the veins of its shell. When it lowers its horn and scrapes the ground it will charge, and whatever its horn catches it hurls away and up into the air. Climbing out of reach will not save you: it can fly.
	}

	DragoneteMiudo: {
		DisplayName: Dragonete Miúdo
		Bestiary: A baby dragon of the Underworld, still more head than wings. It keeps its distance and spits bolts of fire, and if one misses it loses its temper and comes flying in to bite. Its bite is worse than its bark.
	}

	Cogscorpion: {
		DisplayName: Cogscorpion
		Bestiary: "A palace guardian built like a scorpion, its bronze plates edged in red lacquer. It raises its tail before it strikes: the jade at the tip glows brighter until the sting whips over its head, and whoever it touches starts turning to stone."
	}

	FlyingBuddhaHead: {
		DisplayName: Flying Buddha Head
		Bestiary: The head of a great golden statue, cut from its body and kept aloft by Coghaven's machinery, its halo still turning. It drifts after intruders in perfect calm and never strikes in passing. When its eyes open, it drops like a temple bell, and needs a moment to collect itself.
	}
	Mechromancer: {
		DisplayName: Mechromancer
		Bestiary: A robot necromancer that only walks the earth under a blood-red moon, though it has no legs to walk with. A brass skull grins out of the shadow of its horned hood, its claws burn with soul fire, and its mechanical eyes drift around it, never once looking away from you. Where it points, the ground opens and the dead climb out.
	}
}

