Combinator: {
	Title: The Combinator

	Base: Base

	Augment: Augment

	Product: Product

	Combine: Combine

	Separate: Take apart

	Name: "Name:"

	InputTip: Put a weapon here

	ProductTip: The combined weapon comes out here. Put one back to rename it or take it apart

	StatusEmpty: Put a base and an augment weapon in

	StatusReady: Makes {0} damage, {1} use time

	StatusProduct: Rename it, or take it apart

	TooltipParts: Combination of {0} (augment) and {1} (base)

	TooltipAlt: "Right click: the attack of {0}"

	Refusal: {
		NotAWeapon: Only weapons can be combined
		Summon: Summon weapons can't be combined
		AlreadyCombined: Combined weapons can't be combined again
		DifferentClass: Both weapons must be of the same class
	}

	Trait: {
		Homing: Its shots home in on enemies within {0} tiles
		AreaBurst: Its hits burst for {0}% damage over {1} tiles
		AmmoSaver: "{0}% chance not to consume ammo"
		BonusVsMechanical: "{0}% more damage to machines"
		Debuff: "{0}% chance to inflict {1} for {2} seconds"
		TarPlague: Inflicts the Tar Plague for {0} seconds
		JadeCurse: Lays the jade curse
		Stun: "{0}% chance to stun basic enemies for {1} seconds"
		FirstStrike: x{0} damage on the first hit against each enemy
		Pierce: Its shots pierce {0} more enemies
		ArmorPierce: Ignores {0}% of enemy defense
	}

	Help:
		'''
		How the Combinator works
		Put a weapon in Base and another in Augment, then press Combine.
		Both must be of the same class (melee, ranged, magic, Mechanist...). Summon weapons and weapons already combined can't go in.
		The Augment gives the attack: its projectile and its animation.
		The Base gives its passive effects and bonuses (homing, bursts, ammo saving, extra damage to machines...), its crit and its range.
		Damage, use time and mana or steam cost are half the sum of the two. Their reforges are ignored; the new weapon can be reforged at the Goblin Tinkerer like any weapon of its class.
		Right click uses the Base's right-click attack if it has one, otherwise the Augment's.
		Put a combined weapon in the Product slot to rename it or take it apart: both weapons come back as they went in.
		'''
}
